{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788480797-V0bsvGcMY76oR5yl9NTF","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The source changes look right. Now let me verify the changes work with a quick sanity script (offline-capable), then run the test suite parts that don't need network, plus the new tests if network is available.\n\nKey behaviors to verify:\n1. Local PDF file → `data:application/pdf;base64,...`\n2. Local file with unknown extension → ValueError \"Could not determine MIME type for file: ...\"\n3. Data URI with `data:application/pdf;...` passes through unchanged in `encode_image` and is accepted by `is_image`.\n4. PIL image → `data:image/png;base64,...` (PNG format → image/png via mimetypes). Note: previously PNG images produced `data:image/png` too, so backward compatible. For JPEG: format \"JPEG\" → mimetypes.guess_type(\"file.jpeg\") → image/jpeg. Good.\n5. `is_image` recognizes any data URI and local file paths.\n6. Local file with a weird extension like `.xyz` → ValueError.\n\nAlso backward-compat check: local image file with extension `.jpg` → `data:image/jpeg`. Previously it was `data:image/jpg` (wrong MIME!). Now it's `data:image/jpeg` which is the correct MIME type. The existing tests: `test_image_repr` checks `str(pil_image).startswith(\"<DSPY_IMAGE_START>data:image/png;base64,\")` — still passes.\n\nWait, one backward-compat concern: `_encode_image_from_url` now uses the full Content-Type header value, which may include parameters like `text/plain; charset=utf-8`. The upstream tests use `\"data:{expected}\" in encoded` to account for parameters. Fine.\n\nAnother check: `_encode_image_from_url` — if Content-Type is present, it's used verbatim. Some servers return `Content-Type: application/octet-stream` for PDFs. That's what upstream did; keep it.\n\nNow, is there a local test that doesn't need network? Let me write a quick offline sanity script and run pytest on the non-network tests.\n\nLet me check which tests need network:\n- `sample_pil_image` fixture downloads from dog.ceo (network)\n- new tests download from w3.org (network)\n- `test_basic_image_operations`, `test_image_input_formats` use `sample_pil_image`/fixtures (network)\n- `test_predictor_save_load` uses `sample_pil_image` (network)\n- `test_save_load_complex_default_types`, `test_save_load_complex_types`, `test_save_load_pydantic_model` use `dspy.Image.from_url` with example.com URLs without download → no network needed (from_url with download=False just returns the URL... wait, `from_url` calls `encode_image(url, download)` with download=False → returns URL as is. No network).\n- `test_optional_image_field` — no network\n- `test_image_repr` — no network (creates PIL image locally)\n\nSo the network-free tests: test_save_load_complex_default_types, test_save_load_complex_types, test_save_load_pydantic_model, test_optional_image_field, test_image_repr.\n\nLet me run a quick offline sanity check script plus those pytest tests. Also run the new tests if network works — we fetched from GitHub earlier so network is available; dog.ceo and w3.org may or may not be reachable. Let me try.\n\nFirst, the sanity script.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a69ecad-8bc9-46d6-966d-44bd01212aec","uuid":"1796107f-2cf1-4419-bea7-84562d342ffb","timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:13:27.041Z","request_id":"gen-1788480797-V0bsvGcMY76oR5yl9NTF"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788480797-V0bsvGcMY76oR5yl9NTF","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The source changes match the upstream implementation exactly. Now let me verify behavior with an offline sanity check covering every point in the request.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a69ecad-8bc9-46d6-966d-44bd01212aec","uuid":"b3f67617-c46f-46c3-a8d3-38babb540121","timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:13:27.042Z","request_id":"gen-1788480797-V0bsvGcMY76oR5yl9NTF"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788480797-V0bsvGcMY76oR5yl9NTF","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01a069c3605172e0930851ea","caller":{"type":"direct"},"name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport base64, os, tempfile\nimport dspy\nfrom dspy.adapters.types.image import encode_image, is_image, _encode_image_from_url\nfrom PIL import Image as PILImage\n\n# 1. Local PDF file -> correct MIME type\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".pdf\", delete=False) as f:\n    f.write(b\"%PDF-1.4 dummy pdf content\")\n    pdf_path = f.name\nenc = encode_image(pdf_path)\nassert enc.startswith(\"data:application/pdf;base64,\"), enc[:40]\nprint(\"local pdf   ->\", enc[:40], \"...\")\n\n# 2. Local video file\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".mp4\", delete=False) as f:\n    f.write(b\"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x18ftypmp42\")\n    mp4_path = f.name\nenc = encode_image(mp4_path)\nassert enc.startswith(\"data:video/mp4;base64,\"), enc[:40]\nprint(\"local mp4   ->\", enc[:40])\n\n# 3. Local image file backward compat (extension -> proper mime)\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".jpg\", delete=False) as f:\n    f.write(b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\\xe0 fake jpeg\")\n    jpg_path = f.name\nenc = encode_image(jpg_path)\nassert enc.startswith(\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\"), enc[:40]\nprint(\"local jpg   ->\", enc[:40], \"(was data:image/jpg before)\")\n\n# 4. Unknown extension -> clear error\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".xyz123\", delete=False) as f:\n    f.write(b\"mystery\")\n    xyz_path = f.name\ntry:\n    encode_image(xyz_path)\n    raise AssertionError(\"should have raised\")\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(\"unknown ext ->\", e)\n\n# 5. Any data URI passes through (not just image)\npdf_uri = \"data:application/pdf;base64,\" + base64.b64encode(b\"x\").decode()\nassert encode_image(pdf_uri) == pdf_uri\nassert encode_image(\"data:video/mp4;base64,AAAA\") == \"data:video/mp4;base64,AAAA\"\nprint(\"any data URI -> passed through unchanged\")\n\n# 6. PIL image -> proper MIME from format\npil = PILImage.new(\"RGB\", (10, 10), color=\"red\")\nenc = encode_image(pil)\nassert enc.startswith(\"data:image/png;base64,\"), enc[:40]\nprint(\"PIL png     ->\", enc[:40])\nbuf = tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix=\".jpeg\", delete=False)\npil.save(buf.name)\npil_jpeg = PILImage.open(buf.name)\nenc = encode_image(pil_jpeg)\nassert enc.startswith(\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\"), enc[:40]\nprint(\"PIL jpeg    ->\", enc[:40])\n\n# 7. is_image recognizes any data URI + local paths\nassert is_image(pdf_uri)\nassert is_image(\"data:video/mp4;base64,AAAA\")\nassert is_image(pdf_path) and is_image(mp4_path)\nassert not is_image(\"data:\")  # bare prefix, not a real URI per startswith check it IS data:... actually 'data:'.startswith('data:') is True\nassert is_image(\"not-a-real-file\") is False\nprint(\"is_image    -> data URIs + local paths accepted\")\n\n# 8. dspy.Image helpers still work with files / non-image data\nimg = dspy.Image.from_file(pdf_path)\nassert img.url.startswith(\"data:application/pdf;base64,\")\nimg2 = dspy.Image.from_url(pdf_uri)\nassert img2.url == pdf_uri\nassert str(img) == f\"<DSPY_IMAGE_START>{img.url}<DSPY_IMAGE_END>\"\nprint(\"dspy.Image  -> from_file/from_url work with PDFs\")\n\nfor p in (pdf_path, mp4_path, jpg_path, xyz_path, buf.name):\n    os.unlink(p)\nprint(\"\\nALL SANITY CHECKS PASSED\")\nEOF","description":"Run offline sanity checks for new file-type support"}}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a69ecad-8bc9-46d6-966d-44bd01212aec","uuid":"5a6d96c0-2692