{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788480863-9HScE7nfBfYSO172F1Bc","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The work is done. Let me summarize concisely for the user.\n\nSummary of what changed in `dspy/adapters/types/image.py`:\n\n1. `encode_image` now accepts any file: any `data:` URI passes through (not just `data:image/`), and unsupported string errors say \"Unsupported file string\".\n2. `_encode_image_from_file` — reads file, detects MIME via `mimetypes.guess_type` (standard file type detection), raises `ValueError(\"Could not determine MIME type for file: ...\")` if unknown.\n3. `_encode_image_from_url` — downloads, uses `Content-Type` header verbatim; falls back to `mimetypes.guess_type` on the URL; raises `ValueError(\"Could not determine MIME type for URL: ...\")` if neither works.\n4. `_encode_pil_image` — saves with the image's format and maps format → MIME via `mimetypes.guess_type(f\"file.{ext}\")` (e.g. JPEG → image/jpeg), raising a clear error for unknown formats.\n5. `is_image` — now recognizes any data URI and any local file path (\"valid media file reference\"), keeping PIL/URL checks.\n\nBehavior notes:\n- Backward compatible; one visible improvement: local `.jpg` files previously produced the invalid `data:image/jpg` — now correct `data:image/jpeg`.\n- Files keep working through `dspy.Image.from_file`/`from_url`/`from_PIL` and the existing serialization (`<DSPY_IMAGE_START>...<DSPY_IMAGE_END>` tag expansion in ChatAdapter), so models like Gemini/Anthropic that accept PDFs/videos can receive them.\n\nTests: added the 4 new tests in tests/signatures/test_adapter_image.py (PDF from URL with download, mixed MIME types, MIME from response headers, PDF from file). Full run: 56 passed, 2 xfailed (pre-existing) across tests/signatures/ + tests/adapters/.\n\nShould I mention I didn't commit? The user didn't ask for a commit, so leave changes uncommitted.\n\nI don't think memory writes are warranted here — this is a single-task code change; nothing durable about the user's preferences was revealed. Skip memory.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a69ecad-8bc9-46d6-966d-44bd01212aec","uuid":"30afa3af-c3b4-4576-a0da-92de09eea9ef","timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:14:29.843Z","request_id":"gen-1788480863-9HScE7nfBfYSO172F1Bc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788480863-9HScE7nfBfYSO172F1Bc","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The change generalizes `dspy/adapters/types/image.py` from image-only to arbitrary file types, verified against the full test suite.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`dspy/adapters/types/image.py`**\n\n- **`encode_image`** (dspy/adapters/types/image.py:99) — now passes through *any* `data:` URI, not just `data:image/`, so `data:application/pdf;base64,...` and `data:video/mp4;base64,...` flow through unchanged. Unsupported strings now error with `\"Unsupported file string: ...\"`.\n- **`_encode_image_from_file`** (dspy/adapters/types/image.py:132) — reads any local file and detects its MIME type with `mimetypes.guess_type` (standard file-type detection). Raises `ValueError(\"Could not determine MIME type for file: ...\")` when detection fails.\n- **`_encode_image_from_url`** (dspy/adapters/types/image.py:146) — downloads the content and uses the response's `Content-Type` header; if absent, falls back to URL-based `mimetypes.guess_type`, raising `ValueError(\"Could not determine MIME type for URL: ...\")` if neither yields a type.\n- **`_encode_pil_image`** (dspy/adapters/types/image.py:165) — maps the PIL image's format to a proper MIME type via `mimetypes.guess_type(f\"file.{ext}\")` (e.g. JPEG → `image/jpeg`) instead of assuming, with a clear error for undetectable formats.\n- **`is_image`** (dspy/adapters/types/image.py:188) — now accepts *any* data URI and any local file path as a valid media reference, keeping the existing PIL-image and URL checks.\n\nEverything flows through the existing `dspy.Image` interface (`from_file`, `from_url`, `from_PIL`, serialization and `<DSPY_IMAGE_START>` tag expansion), so PDFs, videos, etc. work with models like Gemini and Anthropic that accept them. All prior image behavior is preserved — one visible improvement: a local `.jpg` previously produced the invalid `data:image/jpg` and now yields the correct `data:image/jpeg`.\n\n**`tests/signatures/test_adapter_image.py`** — added 4 tests: PDF from URL with download, mixed MIME types (PDF + JPEG), MIME detection from response headers, and PDF from a local file (used in a predictor end-to-end).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Offline sanity script covering PDF/MP4/JPEG local files, unknown-extension error, arbitrary data-URI passthrough, PIL PNG/JPEG encoding, and `is_image` behavior — all pass.\n- `pytest tests/signatures/ tests/adapters/` — **56 passed, 2 xfailed** (the xfails are pre-existing) in 3.89s, including the new tests which fetch real PDFs from the network.\n\nChanges are uncommitted, matching the working-tree state you started from.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Together","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a69ecad-8bc9-46d6-966d-44bd01212aec","uuid":"7d8913f4-4b00-4edb-af65-350015fa5844","timestamp":"2026-09-04T00:14:38.536Z","request_id":"gen-1788480863-9HScE7nfBfYSO172F1Bc"}
